   "source": [
    "## \u00a78 Cell-type annotation \u2014 plain Leiden + atlas assignment\n",
    "\n",
    "Neither the clustering parameters nor the cell types are chosen here.\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **\u00a78a Clustering.** One Leiden partition of the HCG Harmony embedding \u2014\n",
    "   `n_neighbors = 20`, `resolution = 0.3`, `random_state = 0`. No consensus over\n",
    "   repeats, no `min_cluster_size` filter, no supervised merging. Every cell is\n",
    "   assigned; there are no outliers. \u2192 10 clusters.\n",
    "2. **\u00a78b Atlas assignment.** Each cluster is matched to the CEMBA isocortex\n",
    "   major type with which its genome-wide gene-body mCG profile correlates most\n",
    "   strongly (Spearman, top 3,000 variable genes, per-gene centred within each\n",
    "   dataset). No marker genes are selected and no threshold is applied, so the\n",
    "   **number of cell types is an outcome, not an input.** \u2192 10 cell types.\n",
    "3. **\u00a78c Final labels.** The clusters are relabelled by their arg-max atlas type\n",
    "   and the correlation is shown as a heatmap. There is no outlier-rescue step:\n",
    "   plain Leiden leaves nothing to rescue.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Cell types (10):** IT-L2/3, IT-L4, IT-L5/6, CT-L6 (Exc); Inhib (Inh);\n",
    "ODC, OPC, ASC, MGC, PC/EC.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Why plain Leiden and not consensus clustering\n",
    "\n",
    "Consensus clustering (200 Leiden runs reconciled at `consensus_rate = 0.7`)\n",
    "deliberately over-clusters, and on this dataset that surfaced a 21-cell NP-L6\n",
    "group \u2014 too small to carry through the Hi-C analyses. A 48-configuration sweep\n",
    "(`resolution_exploration.ipynb`) established that **no** consensus setting\n",
    "removes NP-L6 while keeping the inhibitory subtypes and ODC/OPC apart, and that\n",
    "raising `min_cluster_size` retires NP-L6 into IT-L5/6, which the atlas\n",
    "contradicts. Plain Leiden at k = 20, resolution 0.3 dissolves it naturally, 20\n",
    "of its 21 cells joining CT-L6, with no hand-merge.\n",
    "\n",
    "**The cost, stated plainly:** Pvalb and Vip merge into one inhibitory group, and\n",
    "47 cells previously called IT-L2/3 move into IT-L5/6.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Three naming decisions\n",
    "\n",
    "- **IT-L5/6** \u2014 IT-L5 and IT-L6 are not separable here. The margin between them\n",
    "  is 0.007, it flips with the gene set or the similarity metric, and no gene-body\n",
    "  marker distinguishes the cluster in either mCG or GCH. The name spans both\n",
    "  rather than claiming one. Bootstrapping over genes puts IT-L5 or IT-L6 first in\n",
    "  100% of resamples and IT-L4 in 0%, so the *label* is secure even though the\n",
    "  layer is not.\n",
    "- **Inhib** \u2014 this cluster is 48 Pvalb + 85 Vip by the earlier annotation, i.e.\n",
    "  Vip is the majority. It must **not** be called Pvalb; the MGE-Pvalb arg-max\n",
    "  only reflects that a merged inhibitory profile sits closest to that reference.\n",
    "- **PC/EC** \u2014 one cluster holding both pericytes and endothelial cells, so the\n",
    "  joint vascular label is kept.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Free parameters that remain**, to be stated in the Methods rather than implied\n",
    "away: `n_neighbors = 20` and `resolution = 0.3` (chosen to dissolve NP-L6 while\n",
    "retaining the other distinctions \u2014 see the sweep); the embedding beneath\n",
    "everything (250 kb bins, \u226520% coverage filter, `impute.knn` k=10, the leading\n",
    "9 SVD components, Harmony on replicate); and the correlation filters (\u2265100 reads\n",
    "per cluster-gene, 3,000 variable genes, isocortex atlas candidates with \u226540\n",
    "cells). Assignments are unchanged over 500\u201318,295 genes, random gene subsets,\n",
    "and Spearman / Pearson / Kendall / Jaccard."
   ]
